// King's royal decree — Plan G `cast { duration: ... telegraph: ... }`
// block. The cast block lowers to:
//   * EffectOp::CastBegin in `effects` (kind=46, dispatched as
//     EffectKindId::EffectCastBeginApplied = 77)
//   * `pending_program` populated from the `effect { ... }` body —
//     a heal 0 placeholder so the lowering captures *something*
//     non-empty in pending_program (the .sim's ResolveDecree rule
//     fires the actual decree-reset, NOT this pending_program; same
//     MVP shortcut firebolt_probe documents).
//   * `telegraph_kind = TelegraphKind::Circle (= 1)`
//   * `telegraph_params[0] = 12.0` (radius)
//
// AbilityId 4 (alphabetical: last of the four).
//
// Why a placeholder pending_program rather than the actual reset
// effect? The reset is a spatial fan-out (clear evidence on every
// nearby agent), which the registry-driven pending_program dispatch
// can't model today (single-target dispatch only). The .sim's
// ResolveDecree rule does the fan-out via a per-agent scan keyed on
// `agents.busy_until_tick` elapsing.

ability RoyalDecree {
    target: self
    cooldown: 6s
    hint: utility

    cast { duration: 6t telegraph: circle(self.pos, radius: 12) }
    effect { heal 0 }
}
